The original reads the member `type` twice when it is valid: once in the comparison and once in the return. This version reads it into a local once and reads `profile` once. It adds a `__builtin_expect` hint so the common case of an already-set `type` stays on the straight-line path. Behavior is unchanged for every input.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const auto* p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```